","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"assigned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2024-01-18T14:29:34Z","assignee":{"login":"mkouba","id":913004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzAwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba","html_url":"https://github.com/mkouba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1899930331","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/38280#issuecomment-1899930331","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/38280","id":1899930331,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCFbutM5xPqLb","user":{"login":"mkouba","id":913004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzAwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba","html_url":"https://github.com/mkouba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-19T07:57:51Z","updated_at":"2024-01-19T07:57:51Z","body":"> The it is easy to filter out using skip(\"it\") but I think it should always be ignored from the args list, it is an artificial arg (I don't see any use case where you would want the it in the args).\r\n\r\nAgreed.\r\n\r\n> sometime you want to skip them all because you only want to keep the key=value args => skipKeyOnlyArgs()\r\n\r\nThe problem with `skipKeyOnlyArgs()` is that in qute the single identifier is not actually a _key_ but a _value_ and the key/name is defaulted. So for example, `{#myTag foo}` becomes `{#myTag foo=foo}` and then `foo` is resolved from the current context and can be accessed in the tag using `{foo}`. \r\n\r\nIn other words, `foo=foo` is not the same as `foo=\"foo\"`, i.e. it does not mean that `{foo}` outputs `foo` in the tag. We deciced that in order to achieve the behavior of `foo=\"foo\"` with a single identifier we will modify the behavior for string literals used as value-only arguments, i.e. `\"foo\"` will become `foo=\"foo\"`. So that `{#myTag \"foo\"}` becomes `{#myTag foo=\"foo\"}` and `{foo}` outputs `foo` in the tag template.\r\n\r\nNow back to the `skipKeyOnlyArgs()` method - the name is not correct. We could add something like `skipValueOnlyStringLiteralArgs()` but I don't think it's very comprehensible. It might make sense to add something like `skipIdenticalKeyValue()`...\r\n\r\n> sometime you want to only skip the first one because it's consumed as it => skipIt and you want to print the other one (for example readonly=\"readonly\").\r\n\r\nGiven the fact that we always add a defaulted key even for the first unnamed arg and we will remove the `it` binding I'd say that it's always better to use the `_args.skip(\"foo\")`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1899930331/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"mkouba","id":913004,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMzAwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/913004?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba","html_url":"https://github.com/mkouba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mkouba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1899938436","html_url":"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/38280#issuecomment-1899938436","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/38280","id":1899938436,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCFbutM5xPsKE","user":{"login":"ia3andy","id":2223984,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjM5ODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy","html_url":"https://github.com/ia3andy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-01-19T08:04:05Z","updated_at":"2024-01-19T08:04:23Z","body":"> Given the fact that we always add a defaulted key even for the first unnamed arg and we will remove the `it` binding I'd say that it's always better to use the `_args.skip(\"foo\")`.\r\n\r\nYou don't know the name which will be used, it could be anything, so there is no way to filter it:\r\nex: `{#gravatar email size='mm' readonly/}` one could also use `{#gravatar user.email size='mm' readonly/}` or `{#gravatar \"foo@bar.io\" size='mm' readonly/}`\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/1899938436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ia3andy","id":2223984,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjM5ODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ia3andy","html_url":"https://github.com/ia3andy","followers_url":"htt